Prove migration equivalence and enforce effect-based ownership. Boundary checks reject migrated backend-fact snapshots, renamed replacement-state results, backend construction of UI-only state and new backend implementation dependencies. UnlockedData is only for backend-affecting facts that are or may become visible; pure appearance/interaction lives in tui-specific files on the tui-thread without locks/UnlockedData, with drafts frontend-only until string submission. Allow frontend-local/internal copies and legitimate actions/ordered interactions by actual ownership, not a blanket Snapshot word ban. Reconcile every inventory row with migrated ownership, local ownership or an explicit retained-path classification and tests.

Scope the no-Snapshot completion criterion to migrated ordinary backend facts. Explicitly exclude inventoried existing history/streaming and interactive exchanges, including permission/question popups, plugin requests, subagent/inspector/control, branch confirmation and related request/completion interfaces. Preserve their existing protocol-specific state, dependencies, authority, ordering and functionality. History collection access and the user's first backend-requested reply popup require separate designs; no new journal, popup protocol or pending-request UnlockedData belongs here. Checks must prevent using these exceptions to retain unrelated active-agent/directory/model/token bypasses. Verify true selected-agent authority and next-Enter dispatch, workspace root/current directory, execution model/variant/reasoning and tokens. UI labels cannot stand in for authority.

Verify registration, update-during-refresh, independent/dependent flags, identical writes, generation coherence, rapid replacement, stale completion, cancellation and teardown. Migrated render paths must not read backend files, recompute statistics or reach Session/coordinator objects. Prove /exit no longer redundantly publishes statistics and model/context updates refresh independently. Build the existing canonical debug-enabled tree, run full credential-free CTest and applicable module/debug/API guards, complete opt-in tmux wave and targeted PTY coverage. Record real results and rerun commands for blockers, never counting skips as passes. Format changed C++ and run git diff --check. Document publication/local ownership and exact deferred history boundaries. Completion removes superseded in-scope transfers without dual authorities while preserving the explicit deferred transport.

Use the complete ownership/action/result and retained-interface matrices in /05/01/05/Result.md as the acceptance checklist. Retained boundaries include interactive exchanges as well as history, with protocol-specific state, types and synchronization; do not fail completion for those precise pre-existing dependencies or enforce a blanket ban on Snapshot/backend headers. Conversely, do not exempt all of runtime.h or a directory and thereby allow new ordinary-state bypasses. Test the selected changed-flag consumption ownership, not unimplemented multi-subscriber semantics. Require generations only where the implemented normal-runtime path needs them. Startup/normal actions/Enter dispatch are primary acceptance cases; shutdown and /exit are bounded compatibility checks, not justification for speculative framework work.

Apply Proposal.md's explicit decisions rather than rejected sketches: no trust wrapper/projection; no eager /models or /scoped-models lists or scope snapshot/accessor; no whole prompt bundle wrapping; no FrontendDataIndices, SessionFrontendBinding or replacement registry. Trust/on-demand settings delivery and image/editor/Mermaid service APIs are retained exceptions too. Verify individual user approval of resource/completion/session-metadata/todo declarations before treating them as required migration domains. Group cohesive canonical data without speculative lock splitting; aliases remain adjacent to their values, not in per-domain _ts headers.

Check exact source mapping and initialization before display: whole ModelInfo plus optional ReasoningSelection; whole session::Stats including separate active-context/system-prompt estimates; whole Directories; observed Git string; nested PromptModeAndContextSources mode and vector size only; existing store options for session identity; selected-agent name/provenance/tool preset only. No duplicate backend mode/count/identity or copied prompt bodies. Document canonical source members and distinguish derived count/path/total caches from exact member copies. Verify safe diagnostics, no references escaping guards, unregistered detached copies and destination address/index retention on assignment. Tests include dirty-but-display-unchanged writes, count same-size changes, known zero versus absence, independent flag consumption and the existing numeric context-window dependency; do not add speculative typed refresh APIs or cross-domain transactions.

Later user decisions supersede historical proposal names/placement: infrastructure and projections are ava::frontend under src/ava/frontend; session::Stats_ts is adjacent to Stats in session/Stats.h; frontend PromptModeAndContextSources replaces PromptMetadata and refresh names follow current code. No configured primary is automatically inferred from model identity: the accepted nonoptional no-configured-primary definition is named "none", while explicit --agent resolves its configured definition. Verify display matches that canonical value and actual prompt/tool behavior, without fabricating a configured-agent default or duplicating base instructions. Preserve failed-reconstruction execution blocking and recovery separately from legitimate empty prompts; boundary checks must not undo that /03 behavior.
